The host above is an illustrative configuration placeholder, not a measured network address. Configure the actual build server first; this tester does not invent server configuration endpoints. Repeat network case with `http://127.0.0.1:8080/`. With no base URL runner serves app/ read-only on an ephemeral loopback port; no app code is inspected to derive expectations. External server should serve app/ at supplied base; include trailing slash. Fresh browser storage per case. Failures exit nonzero; no skipped/expected-failure cases. No reports/screenshots/dependencies are written.

Public `#screen`, `#rp-link`, `#tm-login-mobile`, `#c`, `#medicines-list` and `window.__tm.clock.fastForward` follow entry-journeys/Contract. Details/summary follows folding-row semantics. Test-list buttons, drawer opener name matching Review/Demo/Controls, reference titles, frame-ancestor inference, Home availability button sequence and pending-medicine clicks are **unverified public UI adapters**, not additional product decisions. If markup exposes equivalent roles or reference popovers, report and correct adapter only, preserving expected behavior. Happy-path fast-forward waits on visible Confirm rather than mutating story; it intentionally does not force outcomes. No private state reads/writes or screen/core imports.

Validation performed for this delivery: node syntax check and complete inventory import. Browser execution not performed; no claim that current app passes. Build thread records each executable ID and each eye case as pass/fail with evidence, resolves adapter discrepancies against Contract, and supplies manual acceptance evidence. Brief:63 existing checks, before/after screenshots and publishing are build-owner tasks outside this tester's write scope.
# Run A0 — Codex test disputes (for the main thread to rule on)

Codex wrote `tests/codex/run-A0/` from the spec before the build (`codex-tests.md`). Tests are unchanged. Result with the app served by `scripts/serve.sh` (`CODEX_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8092/ A0_NETWORK_HOST=<Mac address>`): **2 pass (A0-summaries, A0-settings), 9 fail; every failure is listed here.** Adapter gaps that were build work were fixed in the app: a space between each row title and its summary, so `^Title\s` matches; the drawer handle comes before the panel in the DOM, so "Review controls" is the first matching button; setting references made unique, so the `title` lookup finds each one; both test lists shown on sign-in and OTP in the drawer ("the same list"); QR quiet zone 2 → 4 modules.

| Test | Why it fails | Spec line | Proposed ruling |
|---|---|---|---|
| A0-layout-1280 / 1440 / 1920 "column top aligns with frame" | The test checks that the **first row's summary** ("Test on phone") is within 3 px of the frame top. The **panel's** top edge is the frame top (0 px at all three sizes: `run-checks` P11, `layout_check --app`); the card header "Review panel" with Reset review sits above the first row. | Brief A0 item 2: "The panel's top edge is the frame's top edge at every desktop size." RULES §7.5: panels "top-aligned with the frame's top edge". | Test is stricter than the spec: measure the panel (card) top, not the first summary. |
| A0-inputs-desktop / phone × sign-in / OTP (4) | `getByRole('button', { name: /0000/ })` is not anchored: "0000" also matches 9000000001–9000000005 (6 buttons), so strict mode fails before any fill. | app-logic §11 table (both lists hold "0000" as a substring). | Test bug: anchor the name (`^0000\b`). Behaviour is covered by `run-checks` P15 (tap fills sign-in 9000000001 → Not registered, OTP 1234) and P16 (drawer). |
| A0-network-link "QR must decode to advertised play URL" | `row.locator('img,canvas,svg').first()` takes the row's **chevron icon** (an svg in the summary, earlier in the DOM), not the QR. The QR itself decodes with the test's own BarcodeDetector method to `http://<Mac address>:8092/?play=3` (probe in this session), and with jsQR from a 160 px screenshot (`run-checks` P7, P17). | Brief A0 item 3. | Test bug: select `#rp-qr svg` (or the largest svg). |
| A0-happy-path | Walks sign-in → Home → case → prescribe → call → Prescription confirmed. Home, case, prescribe and calling are steps 2–5 (Runs A1 / A2), not built in A0; it also clicks a button named "Send code", while the approved sign-in button is "Send OTP" (`messages.json`, approved pictures) and Verify is "Verify & sign in". | Brief run table: A2 "The full Cat4 demo plays end to end". | Out of A0 scope: re-run at the end of A2; change `/Send code/` to the approved label "Send OTP". A0 covers the default story itself (`run-checks` P18: decodes to Cat4, patient answers, over the gate, record over the gate; QR steps end on Prescription confirmed → next case). |
