    53	## Run A0 — shell fixes from Apurva's review (D-97; read it in the decision log)
    54	
    55	Short run. App shell and review tools only, no screen or approved picture changes.
    56	1. **Frame 390 : 844** (`design-system/RULES.md` §7, already updated): `app/shell/shell.css` frame variables. Update the frame assertion in `docs/layout_check.py` (and any test that asserts 9:16, e.g. entry-journeys B8 / F9) to 390 : 844. Also update the desktop frame in the reference pages (`ui-screens/home/home-reference.css`, `ui-screens/case/case-styles.css`, and any other `ui-screens` page with a 9:16 frame). **Prove the approved pictures don't change:** re-capture all of them with the D-94 settings after the edit and compare: 0 px difference. The old `styles.css` stays frozen.
    57	2. **One right-hand control column, top-aligned with the frame:** "Test on phone" becomes the first folding row of the review panel (open by default, collapses like the others; QR, steps, link, Copy link inside), and the left-gutter card is removed. The panel's top edge is the frame's top edge at every desktop size. No row ever pushes another off screen at 1280 × 800 (the panel itself doesn't scroll, per §7.3: rows fold).
    58	3. **QR / play link works from a phone:** when served from `localhost` / `127.0.0.1`, build the link with the Mac's network address and port, with one plain line under the QR ("Phone and Mac on the same Wi-Fi"). On the preview site, use its own address. Test that the link decodes to a non-localhost host when an address is configured. The address comes from the server, so add a tiny `scripts/serve.sh` that starts `python3 -m http.server` on 8080 for `app/` and prints the network URL, after running `copy-shared.sh`.
    59	4. **Default story = happy path:** Cat4, patient answers, call over the gate, record over the gate, so playing straight through ends on Prescription confirmed → next case. Failure choices stay in the panel. Update the default QR steps.
    60	5. **Panel summaries wrap** to two lines instead of being cut off ("Turns on · Unl…").
    61	5b. **Test numbers and codes, visible:** inside the **Sign-in answers** row, a short list built from `app/data/test-numbers.js` (the same data the mock server uses, so it can't drift): each number / code with its result in plain words (app-logic §11 table). Tapping a line fills it into the sign-in or OTP field of the running app. On the phone drawer, show the same list when the current screen is sign-in or OTP.
    62	5c. **Settings made understandable:** rename the row **"Timings and limits"**. Show each value with a plain name ("Valid-call minimum", "OTP lock", "Resend waits", …), its value in seconds or minutes, and a tag **Rule** or **Stand-in** (from `source`), with its reference on hover or tap. Move it and **Event log** to the bottom of the panel under a quiet label "Advanced". Order the panel: Test on phone · Story · Jump to a state · Sign-in answers · Home and case answers · Call simulator · Advanced (Timings and limits, Event log).
    63	6. Checks: all existing checks and tests pass. Screenshots for review in `docs/renders/2026-11-09-build-fast/run-A0/`: desktop at 1280 × 800 and 1440 × 900 (Story open, then Call simulator open), and the frame at 1920 × 1080, each next to a before shot. Push. Set run status "Run A0: waiting for main-thread review" and stop.
